RED v8 at cf2b50b on feat/phase-b-live-wiring. 2 new failing, 234 prior GREEN, pnpm check clean.

Both tests are in `live-wiring.spec.ts` inside the RED-4 `verifyDeleteSafe` describe block, new nested describe "verify_then_delete: materialized name must pass /\S/ before deletion".

Note: the 4-test suite has 2 RED and 2 already-GREEN. The safe:true cases ("Test User" and "A") pass today because the current impl returns safe:true when probes 1+2 are empty — those won't break. The whitespace and empty cases are the new RED.

**The fix** — add Probe 3 to `verifyDeleteSafe` when `op.materializedNameProperty` is set:

```typescript
if (op.materializedNameProperty) {
  const nameProbeUrl =
    `${client.apiBase}/${client.db}/entity?_type.string=${encodeURIComponent(op.parentType)}` +
    `&props=_id,${encodeURIComponent(op.materializedNameProperty)}&limit=200`;
  const nameRes = await fetch(nameProbeUrl, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${client.jwt}` } });
  if (nameRes.ok) {
    const body = await nameRes.json() as { entities?: Array<{ [k: string]: unknown }> };
    const badName = (body.entities ?? []).find((e) => {
      const vals = e[op.materializedNameProperty!] as Array<{ string?: string }> | undefined;
      const str = vals?.[0]?.string ?? '';
      return !/\S/.test(str);
    });
    if (badName) {
      return { safe: false, reason: `entity ${badName._id} has whitespace-only or empty materialized ${op.materializedNameProperty}` };
    }
  }
}
```

Also: `DeletePropertyOp` interface in `diff.ts` needs `materializedNameProperty?: string` added.

And: `computePhaseBDiff` must set `materializedNameProperty: 'name'` on the DELETE_PROPERTY ops for `person.forename` and `person.surname` (the verify_then_delete path).

